<%#
  THE HERO (stage 4, S4-1): the cover on the project's own page — until then `cover_node_id`
  reached only the index card and Home. Reads @cover_node (a LIVE node from the page's one
  PageNodes union; nil when the cover is unset or tombstoned) and @page_thumbs. An image-role
  cover is the picture itself through the blob route; any other cover is its server thumbnail in
  a poll cell, the model page's hero-poster rule; no cover renders NOTHING — a project page is not
  a card, and an empty box under the title would read as a broken image.

  A FIGURE SINCE THE SHOP MANUAL (2026-11-19; its spec §5): the picture in a hairline frame beside the
  head, captioned "Fig. 1" and the file's name. A caption, not a callout: the red numbered disc a
  figure carries in the screens waits for figure numbers (spec §9 and §11.3), so nothing here is
  drawn in the accent.
%>
<% if @cover_node %>
  <% ext = File.extname(@cover_node.name).delete(".").upcase.first(4) %>
  <figure class="project-hero" data-controller="thumbs" data-thumbs-url-value="<%= thumbnails_files_path %>">
    <%# `inline_image?`, NOT the role (tinkerex#285): a .heic cover is an image by role and a broken
        picture as raw bytes; the thumbnail branch below is what shows it. %>
    <% if Maker::FileAttachment.inline_image?(@cover_node.name) %>
      <%= link_to file_path(@cover_node.node_id), class: "project-hero-frame", data: file_open_data do %>
        <%= image_tag blob_file_path(@cover_node.node_id), class: "project-hero-img", alt: @cover_node.name %>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <%= link_to file_path(@cover_node.node_id), class: "file-cell project-hero-thumb", "aria-label": @cover_node.name,
                  data: file_open_data(thumb_cell_data(@cover_node.node_id, ext)) do %>
        <%= render "files/thumb", thumb: @page_thumbs.thumb(@cover_node.node_id), ext_label: ext,
                   url: preview_src(@page_thumbs.thumb(@cover_node.node_id)) %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <figcaption class="project-hero-caption">
      <span class="project-hero-fig">Fig. 1</span>
      <span class="project-hero-name mono muted"><%= @cover_node.name %></span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
<% end %>
